sentences.text:
The phrase "settled possession"
does not carry any special charm or magic in it;
nor is it a ritualistic formula which can be confined in a straitjacket.

The Court laid down the following tests which may be adopted as a working rule for determining the attributes of "settled possession" (SCC p. 527, para 12):
(i) that the trespasser must be in actual physical possession of the property over a sufficiently long period;
(ii) that the possession must be to the knowledge (either express or implied) of the owner or without any attempt at concealment by the trespasser and which contains an element of animus possidendi.
